{"term":"moist","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:50160659996b9e301d","definition":"Characterized by the presence of moisture; not dry; slightly wet; damp.","example":"Will theſe moyſt Trees, / That haue out-liu'd the Eagle, page thy heeles / And skip when thou point'ſt out?","pos":"adj","synonyms":["moisty","bewatered","damp","drenched","dripping","drunk","humid","irriguous","madid","moist","moisty","overwatered","plashy","saturated","soaked","sodden","soggy","soppy","spewy","spongy","squidgy","thoan","thone","undried","watered","waterlogged","watery","wet","wetter than an otter's pocket","wiery"],"antonyms":["unmoist","anhydrous","arid","bone dry","droughty","dry","dry as a bone","exsuccous","parched","sare","sear","sere","unmoist","waterless"],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["moist-adiabatic","moisten","moistened","moistener","moistening","moistful","moistify","moistish","moistly","moist media","moist moment","moistness","moist-proof","moistproof","moist tetter","moist towelette","moisty","overmoist","overmoisten","semimoist","supermoist","ultramoist","unmoist","unmoistenable","unmoistened"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/moist#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:fac4703d50ebb2da26","definition":"Of eyes: wet with tears; tearful; also (obsolete), watery due to some illness or to old age.","example":"[H]aue you not a moiſt eie, a dry hand, a yelow cheeke, a white beard, a decreaſing leg, an increaſing belly? […] and will you yet call your ſelfe yong? fie, fie, fie, ſir Iohn.","pos":"adj","synonyms":["dewy-eyed","misty","teary","weepy","wet","cryey","crysome","lachrymate","lachrymose","larmoyant","maudlin","moist","sobful","tearful","teary","watery","weepy"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["moist-adiabatic","moisten","moistened","moistener","moistening","moistful","moistify","moistish","moistly"